  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1227 PM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nSummer heat continues through at least the next several days as \nridging aloft persists and centers closer to our region during the \nlate week period. A few diurnally driven thunderstorms will again be \npossible near the TX/NM state line on Thursday along the edge of the \nmonsoonal moisture. Some solutions also hint at isolated storms \ncontinuing each day into the weekend as moisture remains trapped \nbeneath the upper ridge, but confidence in this occurring is too low \nfor mentionable PoPs at this time. Otherwise, expect above normal \nhighs in the upper 90s to low 100s to continue through the end of \nthe extended forecast period with no indications of any major \npattern change on the horizon.",
